             :intent "`seon.cache/settle!` counts a miss for every `seon.cache/lookup` claim, so the get-if-present idiom `(seon.cache/lookup kind key (constantly 0) (constantly nil))` and the put idiom `(constantly value)` count misses that did no work: `seon.cluster/stored-derivation-schema-keys` (`:seon.cluster/file-schema-keys` shows 1,080 misses = 2 x 540 for 540 derivations) and `seon.health/derived` (`:seon.health/reads` and `:seon.health/derived`) inflate the `seon.cache/status` counters this system steers by. Add one non-counting read to `seon.cache` (a completed entry's value or nil, the Caffeine `getIfPresent` that `seon.cache/retained` already reads through) and call it at those two owners, or give each file one lookup whose derive derefs a shared delay of the batch pull. Proof: `seon.cache-test/a-presence-probe-counts-no-miss` (the implementer writes first): after the probe on an absent key `(:misses (seon.cache/status))` for the kind is 0, after the real lookup 1; and `seon.cluster-test` asserts a 540-file derivation counts 540 misses, not 1,080."
